WEBVTT

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:18.520
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:30.670
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:37.900
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:45.870
And takes me

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:49.820
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:57.970
To the home of wind

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:02.320
He takes me

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:08.820
I'm sure

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:33.980
On a Spring afternoon of April,

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:39.870
Marilla had left for her Aid meeting, and
Anne was alone at home writing a story,

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:45.530
when a peddler knocked on Green Gables.

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:50.610
Anne remembered what Marilla told her
and didn't let him in.

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:54.360
And looked at his wares on the doorstep.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:57.790
This perfume is used by a famous women.

00:01:57.790 --> 00:02:01.120
And this facial cream called
mademoiselle, came from Paris.

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:03.090
They are very good.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:08.500
What's wrong?

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:10.900
I shouldn't look at them,

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:17.170
because Marilla says that if we put all
of that on the face that God gave to us,

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:20.070
it would be a disastrous sin.

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:22.940
But I don't think so.

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:27.510
What if God gives you a
face that needs makeup?

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:29.520
That's a little unfair.

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:33.870
I agree that God can be
rather unfair sometimes.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:39.020
When I see a girl like you living abundantly,

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:45.750
I can't help to think about
my daughter who is sick in bed.

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:48.910
Oh, is your daughter ill?

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:51.450
Yes, it's terminal.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.590
If I had money, perhaps she could be cured,

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:58.550
but my income is...

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:17.760
Mister, show me what you have.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.530
Really?

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:22.630
I don't have just makeup.

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:24.450
Look, what about this?

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.550
And I have even more stuff.

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:29.130
I have brooches and decorations...

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:33.170
And a very cute pin cushion!

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:36.350
The hair dye?

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:46.500
I guarantee that it is an effective one.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:48.090
Look at the instructions.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:53.990
Once you use it you will have a beautiful
raven black hair quickly enough.

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:55.240
Really?

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.440
I would really have raven black hair?

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:58.640
Don't worry.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:01.820
I once sold one to a girl with carrot red hair...

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:05.260
Just a second, please...

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:07.630
Well... What was I saying?

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:15.320
Oh, yes... I sold one to a girl the other day,
and her hair turned black after she used it.

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:17.370
And it made her happy.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:20.410
Here, see for yourself.

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:23.360
The instructions are clearly stated there.

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:28.320
And I'm only selling it
for seventy-five cents.

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:31.110
What do you think? It's a bargain.

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:33.060
Seventy-five cents?

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:38.090
What's wrong?
Seventy-five cents is too expensive?

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:44.080
No. It's not that. I haven't enough money.
I only have fifty cents.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:50.260
Very well. I'll sell it to you for
fifty cents at a special offer!

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:51.620
Really?

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:55.150
It's almost free,
but it can't be helped.

00:04:55.920 --> 00:05:00.230
But don't tell anyone that I
sold it to you for only fifty cents.

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:03.480
Thank you, mister. I'll go fetch the money.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:56.150
By the way, has that child
been too immersed in the story club?

00:05:56.430 --> 00:06:01.500
And I thought she had recovered
from that concert nonsense.

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:04.570
I know that Anne has many faults,

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:08.220
and I don't have intention of denying that.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:11.620
But I am the one who's bringing her up,

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:13.720
not you, Rachel.

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:17.120
So please, keep your opinions to yourself.

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:20.070
She's actually very helpful.

00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:24.490
Thanks to her, I'm going
home to a briskly snapping wood fire

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:28.470
and a table nicely spread for tea.

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:33.770
Instead of to the cold comfort that
you will be receiving in your house.

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:36.910
My, my, I understand Marilla.

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:40.330
I apologize about the things I said about Anne.

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:45.400
But Marilla, You must not get
excited like that because of your head.

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:49.270
I'm sorry for making you worry.

00:06:49.270 --> 00:06:52.210
I suppose I should see a doctor.

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:57.040
Yes, I agree. After all we are getting old.

00:06:57.160 --> 00:06:58.540
You're right.

00:06:58.540 --> 00:07:02.120
I was too harsh, but please don't mind me.

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:06.550
We are good friends.
I don't mind such trivial matters.

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:08.510
Well, good night, Rachel.

00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:10.520
Good night, Marilla.

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:17.420
Marilla is really pleased with that child.

00:07:40.510 --> 00:07:42.130
Welcome back, Marilla!

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:56.060
I'm back.

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:08.040
Anne! Anne!

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:14.540
Anne!

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:51.920
Goodness!

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:11.370
I'll settle Miss Anne when she comes home.

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:14.770
She's gadding off somewhere with Diana,

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:19.490
writing stories or practicing dialogues
or some such tomfoolery,

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:24.360
and never thinking once about
the time or her duties.

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:27.520
Goodness!

00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:30.770
I can't let her do just what she wants.

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:36.170
Her head is full of nonsense

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:39.250
and there's never any
knowing what shape it'll break out in next.

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:44.080
Just as soon as she grows out of
one freak she takes up with another.

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:47.610
But there!

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:52.400
Here I am saying the very thing I
was so riled with Rachel Lynde for saying earlier.

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:56.480
I didn't like to hear what
Rachel said about Anne.

00:09:56.850 --> 00:09:59.950
I must say, with all her faults,

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:06.420
I never found her disobedient
or untrustworthy before.

00:10:06.490 --> 00:10:08.210
But this time is different.

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:12.860
I told her she was to stay home
this afternoon and look after things.

00:10:14.730 --> 00:10:18.500
Well now, I dunno...

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:23.090
Perhaps you're judging her too hasty.

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:27.590
Don't call her untrustworthy until
you're sure she has disobeyed you.

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:31.710
"Mebbe" it can all be explained.

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:32.830
What is there to explain?

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:35.280
Well... I don't know...

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:39.280
She's not here when I told her to stay!

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:43.990
I reckon she'll find it hard to
explain THAT to my satisfaction.

00:10:44.130 --> 00:10:47.780
Of course I knew
you'd take her part, Matthew.

00:10:48.490 --> 00:10:52.600
But I'm bringing her up, not you.

00:11:18.430 --> 00:11:21.420
Just what is she doing?

00:11:25.300 --> 00:11:27.390
Matthew, do you know where the candle is?

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:31.890
Well now, if it isn't there
then it should be in Anne's room.

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:33.300
Oh, you're right.

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:36.050
She took it to study yesterday.

00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:57.300
Mercy on us, have you been asleep, Anne?

00:11:57.580 --> 00:11:58.670
No...

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:00.810
Are you sick then?

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:02.140
No...

00:12:02.310 --> 00:12:05.920
But please, Marilla,
go away and don't look at me.

00:12:06.460 --> 00:12:08.600
Why can't I look at you?

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:12.130
I'm in the depths of despair

00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:17.210
and I don't care who gets head in class
or writes the best composition.

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:19.840
Little things like that are of no importance now.

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:21.740
What are you saying, Anne?

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:24.730
I don't suppose I'll ever be able
to go anywhere again.

00:12:24.730 --> 00:12:26.880
My career is closed.

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:31.280
Please, Marilla,
go away and don't look at me.

00:12:31.420 --> 00:12:32.400
Anne Shirley,

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:35.210
whatever is the matter with you?
What have you done?

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:38.500
Get right up this minute and tell me.
This minute, I say.

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:40.570
There now, what is it?

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:49.080
Look at my hair, Marilla.

00:12:50.630 --> 00:12:52.360
What have you done to your hair?

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:53.840
Why, it's GREEN!

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:57.340
Yes, it's green!

00:13:07.490 --> 00:13:10.880
I thought nothing could be as bad as red hair.

00:13:11.130 --> 00:13:15.340
But now I know it's ten
times worse to have green hair.

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:20.930
Oh, Marilla, you little know
how utterly wretched I am.

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:25.560
I little know how you got
into this fix, but I mean to find out.

00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:28.860
It's too cold up here.

00:13:29.140 --> 00:13:32.930
Come right down to the kitchen
and tell me just what you've done.

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:48.250
I've been expecting something
queer for some time.

00:13:48.610 --> 00:13:51.530
You haven't got into any scrape
for over two months,

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:54.310
and I was sure another one was due.

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:56.820
I dyed it, Marilla.

00:13:57.560 --> 00:14:00.130
Dyed it! Dyed your hair!

00:14:00.370 --> 00:14:03.920
Anne Shirley, didn't you know
it was a wicked thing to do?

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:06.850
I knew it was a little wicked.

00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:12.200
But I thought it was worth while to be a
little wicked to get rid of red hair.

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:16.920
Besides, I meant to be extra good
in other ways to make up for it.

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:21.690
Well, if I'd decided it was worth while,
I'd have dyed it a decent color.

00:14:21.690 --> 00:14:24.030
I wouldn't have dyed it green.

00:14:24.370 --> 00:14:25.550
Green?

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:29.640
But I didn't mean to dye it green, Marilla!

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:34.400
He said it would turn my hair
a beautiful raven black.

00:14:34.650 --> 00:14:37.450
He positively assured me that it would.

00:14:37.450 --> 00:14:40.280
How could I doubt his word, Marilla?

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:43.260
Who said? Who are you talking about?

00:14:44.170 --> 00:14:46.750
The peddler that was here this afternoon.

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:48.830
I bought the dye from him.

00:14:48.830 --> 00:14:54.430
Anne, how often have I told you never
to let one of those sellers in the house!

00:14:54.430 --> 00:14:57.010
Oh, I didn't let him in the house.

00:14:57.300 --> 00:15:01.170
Then Anne told everything
that happened in the afternoon.

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:02.950
Matthew didn't enter inside the room.

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:07.290
He merely sympathized
with Anne in the next room.

00:15:07.880 --> 00:15:12.990
And oh, Marilla, when I saw the
dreadful color it turned my hair

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:16.340
I repented of being
wicked, I can tell you.

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:19.450
And I've been repenting ever since.

00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:24.170
Well, I hope you'll repent to good purpose.

00:15:26.160 --> 00:15:30.450
And that you've got your eyes opened to
where your vanity has led you.

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:33.050
Goodness knows what's to be done.

00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:38.660
I suppose the first thing is to give your hair a
good washing and see if that will do any good.

00:15:49.040 --> 00:15:51.810
The peddler had certainly spoken the truth

00:15:51.810 --> 00:15:55.290
when he declared
that the dye was an effective one.

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:59.160
Oh, Marilla, what shall I do?

00:15:59.830 --> 00:16:02.800
People have pretty
well forgotten my other mistakes,

00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:05.940
like the liniment cake and setting Diana drunk,

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:10.640
but they'll never forget this.

00:16:10.960 --> 00:16:15.070
They will think I am not respectable.

00:16:19.180 --> 00:16:20.490
Oh, Marilla,

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:25.670
what a tangled web we weave when
first we practice to deceive.

00:16:26.160 --> 00:16:28.840
That is poetry, but it is true.

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:32.400
And oh, how Josie Pye will laugh!

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:37.730
I CANNOT face Josie Pye.

00:16:38.530 --> 00:16:43.550
I am the unhappiest
girl in Prince Edward Island.

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:45.610
Goodness.

00:17:12.290 --> 00:17:13.560
Good morning, Anne.

00:17:16.250 --> 00:17:17.920
You're still not ready for school?

00:17:18.190 --> 00:17:20.430
If you don't hurry we will be late.

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:22.240
Diana...

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:24.720
What's wrong, Anne?

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:34.660
If Josie Pye saw me now,

00:17:34.870 --> 00:17:36.860
I would rather die!

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:42.820
I won't tell anybody about it, Anne.

00:17:43.230 --> 00:17:44.810
I promise solemnly.

00:17:45.170 --> 00:17:46.710
Thank you, Diana!

00:17:47.180 --> 00:17:49.550
You will always be my best friend indeed.

00:17:58.290 --> 00:18:03.500
During that time Anne went nowhere
because of her green hair

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:08.080
and shampooed her hair every day to no avail.

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:13.040
And at the end of the week
Marilla said decidedly:

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:15.610
It's no use, Anne.

00:18:16.010 --> 00:18:18.490
That is fast dye if ever there was any.

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:21.260
Your hair must be cut off.

00:18:21.260 --> 00:18:23.960
You can't go out with it looking like that.

00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:09.980
Do you want me to cut it off?

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:12.680
Please cut it off at once, and have it over.

00:19:21.770 --> 00:19:24.250
I feel that my heart is broken.

00:19:24.420 --> 00:19:26.760
This is such an unromantic affliction.

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:29.270
The girls in books

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:34.840
lose their hair in fevers or sell it
to get money for some good deed,

00:19:35.250 --> 00:19:40.960
and I'm sure I wouldn't mind losing my
hair in some such fashion half so much.

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:45.930
But having to cut your hair off
because you've dyed it a dreadful color

00:19:45.930 --> 00:19:47.710
it's not romantic!

00:19:47.710 --> 00:19:49.180
But do you want it cut?

00:19:49.300 --> 00:19:51.560
Or do you want it left like this?

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:53.300
No. Please cut it off.

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:54.670
But Marilla,

00:19:55.100 --> 00:19:59.180
may I weep
all the time you're cutting it off?

00:20:00.100 --> 00:20:05.020
If it won't interfere,
because It seems such a tragic thing.

00:20:35.390 --> 00:20:38.980
I'll never look at myself
again until my hair grows!

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:45.020
Yes, I will, too.

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:48.120
I'd do penance for being wicked that way.

00:20:50.260 --> 00:20:53.110
I'll look
at myself every time I come to my room

00:20:53.300 --> 00:20:56.430
and see how ugly I am.

00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:59.910
And I
won't try to imagine it away, either.

00:21:00.050 --> 00:21:05.020
I never thought I was vain about
my hair, of all things,

00:21:05.480 --> 00:21:07.670
but now I know I was.

00:21:08.050 --> 00:21:09.820
In spite of its being red,

00:21:09.820 --> 00:21:13.820
because it was so long and thick and curly.

00:21:31.330 --> 00:21:32.580
Good morning, Anne!

00:21:32.650 --> 00:21:33.950
Diana!

00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:43.480
It looks good on you, Anne!

00:21:43.750 --> 00:21:45.190
Don't comfort me.

00:21:45.310 --> 00:21:48.650
I brought a ribbon for you.

00:21:48.770 --> 00:21:49.500
Will you try it?

00:21:50.100 --> 00:21:50.970
A ribbon?

00:21:51.220 --> 00:21:52.900
A black velvet ribbon.

00:21:53.340 --> 00:21:53.960
Look.

00:21:54.240 --> 00:21:58.470
Aunt Josephine gave it to me,
but I'm sure it would suit you more.

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:00.890
Let me tie it for you!

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:05.180
Let's tie it around your
head with a bow at one side.

00:22:06.810 --> 00:22:08.860
Oh, it suits you wonderfully.

00:22:10.700 --> 00:22:11.450
Wait.

00:22:12.720 --> 00:22:14.470
I've brought you a mirror.

00:22:15.700 --> 00:22:16.710
Fits perfectly, doesn't it?

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:18.070
Do you think so?

00:22:18.210 --> 00:22:19.030
Of course.

00:22:19.130 --> 00:22:23.190
Let's tell everyone that
it is Charlottetown's latest fashion.

00:22:26.380 --> 00:22:33.210
Anne's clipped head made a sensation
in school in that Monday.

00:22:33.650 --> 00:22:41.080
And to her relief nobody
guessed the real reason for it.

00:22:41.720 --> 00:22:46.420
It was all thanks to Marilla's skills
by cutting perfectly the green hair

00:22:46.580 --> 00:22:51.730
and Diana's loyalty
in not revealing the secret.

00:22:52.640 --> 00:22:57.790
But Josie Pye, however,
did not fail to inform what she thought.

00:22:58.190 --> 00:23:01.650
Anne, your hair could be the latest fashion,

00:23:01.650 --> 00:23:03.960
but you look like a perfect scarecrow.

00:23:09.290 --> 00:23:11.990
I didn't say anything
when Josie said that to me,

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:17.370
because I thought it was part of my
punishment and I ought to bear it patiently.

00:23:17.860 --> 00:23:22.000
It's hard to be told you look like a scarecrow.

00:23:22.390 --> 00:23:26.950
But the others liked my hair,
all thanks to you and Diana.

00:23:29.060 --> 00:23:35.710
I shall never try to be beautiful again.
Of course it's better to be good.

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:38.330
Just like Mrs. Allan and Miss Stacy.

00:23:38.920 --> 00:23:41.850
And grow up to be a credit to you.

00:23:42.770 --> 00:23:44.990
Marilla, am I talking too much?

00:23:45.150 --> 00:23:47.240
Does it hurt your head?

00:23:47.440 --> 00:23:49.450
My head is better now.

00:23:49.750 --> 00:23:51.670
It was terrible bad this afternoon, though.

00:23:51.980 --> 00:23:54.780
As for your chatter,
I don't know that I mind it.

00:23:54.910 --> 00:23:56.860
I've got so used to it.

00:23:57.470 --> 00:23:59.230
I'll go prepare some tea for you.

00:24:17.990 --> 00:24:19.640
In one summer day,

00:24:19.640 --> 00:24:21.610
Anne is playing by the lake.

00:24:21.700 --> 00:24:24.850
She and her friends started
to perform an outstanding dialogue.

00:24:25.050 --> 00:24:27.750
Next episode of Anne of Green Gables:

